import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Organizational record · America's School Trust Library"
  description="The Library's organizational record: what was filed, when, and by whom — registrations, incorporation, and the board actions that seated the founding board of America's School Trust Library."
  sourceId="organizing"
>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-a:text-blue-700 prose-a:underline">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Organizational record</h1>

    <p class="record-banner">
      <strong>Organizational record</strong> — This page is the Library's
      organizational record — what was filed, when, and by whom. The
      plan-version of this page, written before any of it had happened, was
      superseded August 3, 2026.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>
        This page once described, in the future tense, how the Library would
        become a legal organization. That work is done; the plan-version of
        this page is preserved in the Library's records, superseded August 3,
        2026. What follows is what actually happened.
      </em>
    </p>

    <h2>The record</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>July 10, 2026</strong> — Oregon Department of Justice Charitable
      Activities Registration No. 72571 acknowledged.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 15–16, 2026</strong> — Certificate of name compliance issued
      by the Division of Financial Regulation (corrected copy July 16),
      authorizing use of “Trust” in the corporate name.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 21, 2026</strong> — Articles of Incorporation e-filed with
      the Oregon Secretary of State. Oregon Registry No. 259005891.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>July 30, 2026</strong> — Federal Employer Identification Number
      issued (kept as an internal corporate record).
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>August 3, 2026</strong> — The founding board — David Sullivan,
      President; Barbara K. Sullivan, Treasurer; Kenneth Magee, Secretary —
      seated by unanimous written consent, adopting
      <a href="/bylaws/">Bylaws v7</a>, the
      <a href="/rights/">Constitution and Readers' Bill of Rights v1</a>, and a
      Conflict of Interest Policy v2. All published on the
      <a href="/governance/">governance page</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>August 9, 2026</strong> — The board added Barry Shane as a
      director and accepted the withdrawal of Barbara K. Sullivan. Offices were
      reassigned: David Sullivan, President and Treasurer; Kenneth Magee,
      Secretary. The board now has three directors; two seats remain open.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Open</strong> — the application for federal tax exemption.
      America's School Trust Library is an Oregon nonprofit public benefit
      corporation. The federal tax-exemption process is under way; no
      determination has been issued.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
